  "body": "From some basic testing (https://codepen.io/patrickhlauke/pen/MWJNXXr) it seems that a `<legend>` is correctly recognised and used to provide the accessible name for a `<fieldset>` (in the accessibility tree) regardless of whether it's the *first* child of the `<fieldset>` or not - at least testing in Chrome, Firefox, Safari (macOS). could/should this be reflected in the spec?\r\n\r\nIt seems it still needs to be a child element (so sadly, it's not currently possible to have it at a deeper level / have some other wrapper/container in between) - while I'd love to see this relaxed as well (and allow something more along the lines of `<fieldset><div><legend>...</legend> ... </div></fieldset>`, I don't think there's currently any strong desire from implementations to change this.",
